    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d810">

                <pb facs="0753" n="741" xml:id="pg741"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R./1092: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Nicholson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-18T09:00:00-06:00">May 18, 1940—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 12:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>46. Department’s telegram No. 31, May 17, 7 p.m. Nicaraguan Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs confirms that affirmative reply regarding Uruguayan proposal was sent by
                    telegraph to Panama on May 16.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nicholson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
